From f1b362d4927ba5fe91e27bb49183644e0ac3d1ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelinek <jakub@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:28:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] libgomp: Check for overflows in some cases

Given the https://gcc.gnu.org/pipermail/libstdc++/2026-September/067867.html
changes, I had a brief look at gomp_aligned_alloc and omp_aligned_{,c}alloc.
At least when alignment is power of two, omp_aligned* seems to perform all the
overflow checking they should I think.  gomp_aligned_alloc is used internally,
if it uses posix_memalign or memalign, it relies on libc performing overflow
checking, for the aligned_alloc case it already performs overflow checking
itself.  Given the above libstdc++ change, seems at least Mingw _aligned_alloc
performs no overflow checking, so this patch adds overflow checking for it
(but relies on NULL/EINVAL if al is not a power of two from Mingw/Win).
And for the fallback also adds overflow checking.

2026-09-23  Jakub Jelinek  <jakub@redhat.com>

	* alloc.c (gomp_aligned_alloc): Check for overflows in the
	_aligned_malloc case and in the last fallback.

(cherry picked from commit 04106ce784babdaa721bc1f1cabcdf6f44f45efb)
---
 libgomp/alloc.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libgomp/alloc.c b/libgomp/alloc.c
index 47ff605660f2..34ece6248465 100644
--- a/libgomp/alloc.c
+++ b/libgomp/alloc.c
@@ -82,12 +82,22 @@ gomp_aligned_alloc (size_t al, size_t size)
       ret = NULL;
   }
 #elif defined(HAVE__ALIGNED_MALLOC)
-  ret = _aligned_malloc (size, al);
+  /* Mingw64 doesn't perform overflow checking, so do it ourselves.
+     It does power of two checking though.  */
+  if (__builtin_add_overflow_p (size, al + 2 * sizeof (void *), (size_t) 0))
+    ret = NULL;
+  else
+    ret = _aligned_malloc (size, al);
 #else
   ret = NULL;
   if ((al & (al - 1)) == 0 && size)
     {
-      void *p = malloc (size + al);
+      void *p;
+      size_t sz;
+      if (__builtin_add_overflow (size, al, &sz))
+	p = NULL;
+      else
+	p = malloc (sz);
       if (p)
 	{
 	  void *ap = (void *) (((uintptr_t) p + al) & -al);
